  "published": "2026-11-18T09:59:47Z",
  "modified": "2026-11-18T09:59:47Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-120154: check the ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE target row against RLS\n  policies before evaluating the user-supplied WHERE clause\n- CVE-2026-16237: INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE through an automatically\n  updatable view now fails when the conflicting row is not visible through the\n  view\n- CVE-2026-116311: DROP OWNED BY no longer changes row-level security policies\n  on tables the current user does not own\n- CVE-2026-116327: treat a leaky function applied to a CaseTestExpr or Param as\n  leaky, so it is not evaluated before row-level security quals\n- CVE-2026-120146: REASSIGN OWNED requires the CREATEDB privilege to change the\n  owner of a database, as ALTER DATABASE ... OWNER TO does\n- CVE-2026-116308: dict_int: return NULL for a zero-length token instead of\n  reading past its end\n- CVE-2026-116321: prevent construction of invalid \"name\" values via array\n  element assignment\n- CVE-2026-16240: pg_basebackup: do not use received backup manifest data as a\n  format string\n- CVE-2026-116303: check EXECUTE privilege on the cast functions used by foreign\n  key checks and by to_json()/to_jsonb()",
